{
  "name": "tiger",
  "_about": "THE REFERENCE SCULPT (2026-11-04, docs/engines.md 'the sculpt overlay'): the cat frame's rig, drawn by shapes written for a tiger -- long and low, a deep keel of a chest under heavy shoulder blades, massive forearms on big round paws, a lean loin with the loose belly skin under it, a high rump on thick thighs; a broad head that is mostly cheek, flared with a white ruff, short round ears black behind, a white-padded muzzle on a pink nose; the rig's own long tail kept. Stripes are the coat shader's (coatpat.js): along the body frame on the trunk, across each leg's own on the limbs, stacked on the brow (2026-11-05 review pass, gen: scratchpad sc/carn/gen/tiger.py: the face's markings as seated decals, broader stripes -- patScale 1.28 -- black ear backs with their white spot, ringed tail end, a smaller white jowl and throat) (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), black behind round the white spot (the edge band `rim`), white-furred in the hollow; the roots faired. (2026-11-08, tailframe.py) The tail's stripe frames CONTINUOUS (tools/creaturegen/var/tailframe.py): the root cone and the segments inside it one frame, the rest a frame per few segments, each frame's origin set back by the arc length so the stripes run on across every seam, all measured from the top -- they broke into chevrons at the tail's root, each segment's stripes started afresh. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 16 white whiskers a side, 4 rows on the whisker pad (135-203 mm); 3 white whiskers a side, a brow tuft (49-68 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh). (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/tails.py) The TAIL is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along its bones, not a chain of cones blended one into the next: no beads, its thin end exact rings.",
