  "sculpt": {
    "_about": "x forward, y up, z left, metres, at s = 1; each shape rides the bone it names; `mirror` makes the right one from the left || ROUND 2 (2026-11-07, scratchpad var/tgr.py): the lion's cat face (the L3/L4 shapes) moved on by tX/tY and painted a tiger's; white cheek ruffs (ruffT/ruffP/ruffL); the crown striped in the body's frame; the lion's toe lobes || ROUND 3: the face's own fine marks (cheekS*, eyeLine, browB*, foreLine: thin paint ells deep along the surface's normal), flat round ears orange-rimmed with black backs (earBack) and the white spot, a smaller pink-brick nose || ROUND 4: a bigger, broader head (hs 1.2) with a rounder skull, a short broad muzzle (faceX -0.025, mw 1.4), big white pads and a squarer chin; the jowl ball flattened and the ruff a fringe of three locks (ruffU/P/L) swept back and down, the cheek marks along it; round cat paws in the coat's colour (pawBase/hpawBase and the lion's toe lobes) || ROUND 5: the ruff's locks thick with round tips, blended into the cheek; two broader cheek strokes; the pads pulled back behind the nose; a thin hidden core down each leg in the body's frame (coreFL/coreHL) so the leg stripes' frame never swaps slots on the inside of a leg",
